omaphone began in the omatel repository (https://github.com/derekross/omatel)
and was moved here with its history. It uses omatel's crates
(GPL-3.0-or-later) as dependencies. One of them, omatel-theme, contains
theme support adapted from gliff (https://github.com/omacom/gliff),
Copyright (c) 2026 Kevin McConnell, under the MIT license; that crate's
source carries the license notice, and omatel's NOTICE has its full text.

Parts are taken from omacam (https://github.com/derekross/omacam, the same
author, GPL-3.0-or-later): the journal logging set-up, the window
screenshots for tests, and bin/cross.

Phone follows the behavior and layout of AOSP's Dialer app; no AOSP code
is included. The icons are original artwork.

The omaphone binary links these Rust crates statically, each under its own
license: omatel's crates (GPL-3.0-or-later; omatel-theme partly MIT), gtk4,
gdk4, gsk4, glib, gio, libadwaita and the other gtk-rs crates (MIT), zbus
and zvariant (MIT), rusqlite (MIT), phonenumber (Apache-2.0), chrono (MIT
OR Apache-2.0), serde (MIT OR Apache-2.0), and the crates listed in
Cargo.lock. It links GTK and libadwaita (LGPL-2.1-or-later) and SQLite
(public domain) dynamically.
